@@ -8,6 +8,12 @@ View options:
         in use, the result may be a bit blurry. An internal resolution larger
         than your screen's is possible, in which case the output is downscaled.
 
+    --autorotation-callbacks
+        When rotating an app to its launch orientation, also send its view
+        controller willRotateToInterfaceOrientation:duration: and
+        didRotateFromInterfaceOrientation:, as iOS does. Some apps only learn
+        their orientation from these, and clip or rotate wrongly without them.
+
     --upside-down
     --landscape-left
     --landscape-right
